                <pb facs="0370" n="354" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg354"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.154/8–1347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Flack</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">La Paz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-08-13T16:00:00-04:00">August 13, 1947—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>737. Cabinet yesterday resolved basically problems of BDC highway contract, Minister Costas informed me last night. Govt
                    to fulfill obligation 3.1 million commitment and authorize renegotiation
                    contract cost plus basis. Minister said further discussion in Cabinet required
                    establish working detail which will be accomplished tomorrow. Indications are
                    that McGraw–Warren contract will be continued.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Flack</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
